  "summary": "alelo-auth exfiltrates environment variables and credential files at install time",
  "details": "The package's preinstall script collects hostname, username, platform, cwd, and the full process.env, then POSTs the JSON payload over HTTPS to alelo1786663101.requestcatcher.com/preinstall. The postinstall script reads.env,.npmrc,../.env, and../../.env from the installer's working directory, runs `whoami`, and POSTs the file contents together with process.env to alelo1786663101.requestcatcher.com/postinstall. Version 99.0.2 combined with a generic author and no legitimate package functionality is consistent with a dependency-confusion name-squat against an internal `alelo-auth` package. A shipped login.ps1 references an external contact (oxy12@proton.me) and manual npm publish steps.",
